WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.610
Yuya!

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:03.950
Yuzu!

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:06.000
Yuzu, you're okay?

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.400
Forget about me.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.350
Wh-Where are you going?

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:11.320
The harbor.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.510
Your father...

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.490
Yuya, your father is there!

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:15.160
Father?

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.540
Asuka, enough.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:31.820
Get off the ship.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:34.480
No, I shall go with you.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.120
Only one person is needed.

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:39.990
I promise that I'll convince Leo Akaba.

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:42.750
I told you, it won't work...

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.690
I won't let you go to Academia.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:48.600
Before, you really gave me the slip.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.340
But I won't let you get away again.

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:54.770
In a world split into four dimensions,

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:59.350
four boys exist, all with the same face.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:02.270
Their dragons call to each other,

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:05.560
almost as if seeking one another.

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:43.940
The Great Galaxy Shining in Darkness

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:50.550
Damn! We missed it!

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.810
Is Dad really on that ship?

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:55.050
Yeah, probably.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:56.800
We can still catch up!

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.520
How will you go after him?

00:02:58.520 --> 00:02:59.820
I'm gonna find a ship!

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:00.720
A ship?

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.260
Even a fishing boat would be enough.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:05.900
There must be something we can take!

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:12.910
I shall accept your duel!

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:15.070
Step back, traitor.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:17.340
I'll turn you into a card later.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:20.830
First, I want to settle things 
with my old teacher.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:24.970
You got away from me before, 
but we're surrounded by ocean now.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:26.550
There's nowhere to go.

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:30.260
Which means you have 
to accept. Right, sir?

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.590
I'll take that duel.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:35.280
Kaito!

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.170
Who are you, coming out of nowhere?

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:41.170
I came here in Syun's place, to save Ruri.

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:45.790
Kaito, eh? You were also his student.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:48.370
And Kurosaki's friend.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:53.080
When you lose in your duel to me, 
you must take me to Ruri.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:55.120
Lose? Me?

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:57.340
Sorry, not happening!

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:01.200
After all, weren't you among the 
ones that Academia dominated?

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.820
We were not dominated by Academia.

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:06.210
Academia's army has already 
ceased aggressions

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:08.890
and works to restore the Xyz Dimension

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:12.100
by the decision of Supreme 
Commander Edo Phoenix.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.300
Edo?

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:14.520
Yes.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:19.270
Edo's duel with your son, 
Yuya, opened his heart.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.390
And I, who have fought Academia 
alone for so long,

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:26.510
was also reminded by Yuya 
of the importance of allies.

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:29.130
So I will fight you!

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:31.010
To take back Syun's little sister!

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:32.220
I see...

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:36.830
You're saying Yuya also goaded 
Edo into betraying us, too.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:37.920
Pathetic.

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:39.150
Yuya...

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.240
I get it!

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:43.860
I'll do you the favor of fighting you.

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:48.330
Tearing a student down in his teacher's 
eyes is fun in its own right.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:51.340
And for this occasion, I'll have the teacher

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:54.270
and everyone on the ship witness it.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:59.010
The glorious entertainment duel between 
two of Yusyo Sakaki's students!

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:00.290
Is this all right?

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:05.080
Yes... As an instructor, it's my duty 
to see this through, as well.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:06.830
Now, everyone...

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:11.040
I invite you to watch a super-gorgeous show, 
the likes of which you rarely see,

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.690
even on a first-rate luxury liner like this!

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:17.900
Its name... The Entertainment Duel Show!

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:19.100
Entertainment?

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.300
A duel, as a show?

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.000
What does that mean?

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:27.960
The fighters will be two students, taught by 
peerless entertainer Yusyo Sakaki.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.690
I, Dennis,

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:33.680
and the greatest heel of our age, Kaito!

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:35.100
Who are you calling a heel?

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:36.650
Nonsense!

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:38.170
Don't be that way...

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:41.090
Are you really Yusyo Sakaki's student?

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:44.940
You can't make anyone smile 
with a scowl like that.

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:46.620
Enough talk!

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:48.990
Then, let's begin.

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:50.070
Duel!

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:56.870
I'll start us off beautifully.

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:58.370
My turn!

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:01.950
I set the Pendulum Scale with Scale 2 
Performage Bubble Gardna

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:07.180
and Scale 5 Performage Candy Crafter!

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:16.520
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 3 and 4 simultaneously.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:18.490
Pendulum Summon!

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:21.560
Appear, my monsters!

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:24.300
First, Performage Hat Tricker.

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:26.990
Then, Performage Flame Eater.

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:30.990
Two Level 4s at the same time!

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:35.050
The girl in the front row seems 
to have already caught on.

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:38.530
It's time to bring out the one 
I just can't duel without...

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:43.150
I overlay Level 4 Hat Tricker 
and Flame Eater!

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:50.090
The show must go on!

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:54.990
Sky magician, travel around 
the stage magnificently!

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:56.660
Xyz Summon!

00:06:56.660 --> 00:07:01.800
Come out, Rank 4 Performage 
Trapeze Magician!

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:09.260
I now end my turn.

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:11.290
Next, it's your turn.

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:12.940
Put on a good show, okay?

00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:14.480
My turn.

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:16.770
When no monsters are on my field,

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:21.170
and a monster Special Summoned 
from your Extra Deck is on yours,

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:24.390
I can Special Summon Cipher 
Twin Raptor from my hand.

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:32.130
I also summon Cipher Wing from my hand!

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:36.410
By tributing it, I activate its monster effect.

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:38.590
I increase Twin Raptor's level by 4!

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:43.830
One Twin Raptor can serve 
as two Xyz components.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:48.250
I overlay with my Level 8 Twin Raptor!

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:55.020
Galaxy shining in the darkness...

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:59.080
Dwell within the god of vengeance 
and become my servant!

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:01.160
Xyz Summon!

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:06.890
Descend, Rank 8 Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon!

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:11.800
Looking good!

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.210
I like the whole "demon of vengeance" angle.

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:16.440
You really are giving off a heel vibe.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:19.890
True, if you attack my Trapeze 
Magician with your dragon,

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:21.510
you could destroy it.

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:25.530
But in an entertainment duel, 
that would be boring...

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:28.990
You have to do something that 
will really surprise people.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:32.960
You stole Ruri! Now, I'll steal your monster!

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:39.830
I use one of Cipher Dragon's Overlay 
Units to activate its monster effect!

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:41.750
Cipher Projection!

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:49.010
I negate Trapeze Magician's monster effect, 
to take control of it until the end of my turn.

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:52.200
And it also becomes a 
Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon.

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:56.060
Wow! That's amazing!

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:58.820
You even changed its appearance!

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:02.780
But now, you don't have a 
monster to fight, so...

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:03.310
Huh?

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:05.490
Wait, are you gonna attack me?

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:06.860
Battle!

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:10.540
I attack you directly with my Cipher Dragon!

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:13.200
Annihilating Cipher Stream!

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:16.300
When you attack me directly,

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:19.700
I can Special Summon Performage 
String Figure from my hand.

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:23.110
It will take this battle!

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:32.270
Behold...

00:09:32.270 --> 00:09:37.090
String Figure can't be destroyed by battle, 
and reduces battle damage to 0.

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:45.340
And in that instant, I activate Candy 
Crafter's Pendulum Effect,

00:09:45.340 --> 00:09:47.660
to increase my own life by 1000!

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:56.110
That effect can be activated during your 
turn, when the Battle Phase ends,

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:59.370
and when my Performages 
have fewer attack points

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:02.800
than the monsters on your side of the field do.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:04.620
What a big help!

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:08.240
If you had just attacked Trapeze 
Magician without the effect,

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:10.300
I would've been in big trouble.

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:12.360
Instead, you gave the audience a big thrill!

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:17.030
I set one card and end my turn.

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:21.310
In that instant, Cipher Dragon's 
monster effect ends,

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:23.880
and control of Trapeze Magician reverts to you.

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:29.310
Welcome back, Trapeze Magician.

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:31.340
Now, the real show's about to start.

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:33.610
I'm going to use all the power at my disposal

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:38.250
to give my teacher and the 
audience a real show!

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:50.700
My turn!

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:54.860
I summon Performage Damage 
Juggler from my hand.

00:10:57.190 --> 00:11:00.800
And String Figure's monster effect activates.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:05.680
When this card is used as a component, I can 
Fusion Summon without Polymerization.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:09.650
I fuse Damage Juggler and String Figure.

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:13.330
Acrobat who manipulates pain,

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:16.650
blend into the string of infinite 
shapes, and become

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:19.020
a new witch who can race through the heavens.

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:20.390
Fusion Summon!

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:25.860
Appear, Level 7 Performage Trapeze Witch!

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:29.600
Your partner is finally here, Trapeze Magician.

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:32.620
Now, you can show your real stuff!

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:37.580
I use one of Trapeze Magician's Overlay 
Units to activate its monster effect.

00:11:37.930 --> 00:11:41.810
It lets Trapeze Magician attack 
twice during my turn!

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:43.420
I see.

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:47.550
Use its partner's effect to reduce 
Cipher Dragon's attack points,

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:51.330
then finish me off with continuous 
attacks by Trapeze Magician.

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:53.890
Is that your intention?

00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:55.100
Good guess.

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:57.660
I can tell you studied under Yusyo Sakaki.

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:01.600
But if you've guessed that much, you can 
probably defend against it, right?

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:03.070
I activate my set card!

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:09.270
I activate my trap card Cipher Deterrent, 
targeting Cipher Dragon!

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:14.250
It prevents Cipher Dragon's 
destruction on this turn,

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:17.850
and doubles its attack points during 
the End Phase, after battle occurs!

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:20.640
Wow, what an amazing trap!

00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:24.000
That was a little bit of feigned surprise.

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.300
The fact is, I took that into account.

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:27.270
What?

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:31.770
You may have just dropped in, 
Kaito, but I know all about you.

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:35.150
There were records about you 
in Academia's database...

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:37.850
I had a look through your duel data,

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:41.390
and up until now, this duel has 
all gone according to plan.

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:44.490
It means you're still in the palm of my hand.

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:49.310
I use Trapeze Magician's 
remaining Overlay Unit

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:54.110
to allow Trapeze Witch to attack twice.

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:59.920
Now, behold the spectacular 
flying trapeze show!

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:05.000
Watch the perfect synchronization of these 
two monsters, as they fly through the air!

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:09.700
First, Trapeze Magician attacks 
Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon!

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:14.870
In that instant, Trapeze Witch's 
monster effect activates.

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:17.040
When a Performage does battle,

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:20.310
it lowers the attack points of 
one of your monsters by 600!

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:22.810
Go, Trapeze Magician!

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:30.220
Cipher Deterrent's effect prevents 
Cipher Dragon's destruction!

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:31.820
But you still take damage.

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:38.010
A mere 100 damage isn't much.

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:39.740
I recognize that...

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:42.000
But the second one is going to hurt.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:48.770
Go! Second attack, Trapeze Magician!

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:57.980
Trapeze Witch's effect reduced its 
attack points by another 600!

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:01.060
Even if you avoid destruction, 
you still take damage...

00:14:01.580 --> 00:14:03.190
700 damage.

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:07.010
There's still more to go.

00:14:07.010 --> 00:14:09.360
Now, Trapeze Witch attacks.

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:12.350
Naturally, its monster effect

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:15.700
reduces Cipher Dragon's attack 
points by another 600.

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:19.420
Trapeze Witch has 2400 attack points.

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:23.760
If we subtract Cipher Dragon's 
1200 attack points from that...

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:25.610
Yes, that one's easy.

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:29.080
You take 1200 damage!

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:44.600
Good, good!

00:14:44.600 --> 00:14:47.400
The anger in those eyes. It's thrilling...

00:14:49.600 --> 00:14:53.300
But how long will you be able 
to keep glaring at me?

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:54.890
Enough talk!

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:57.520
Your attack isn't over yet.

00:14:57.520 --> 00:14:58.540
Bring it already!

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:02.090
If you insist.

00:15:02.090 --> 00:15:04.060
My final continuous attack.

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:08.590
Trapeze Witch, attack Galaxy-Eyes 
Cipher Dragon.

00:15:08.950 --> 00:15:12.520
In that instant, Cipher Dragon's 
attack points decrease by 600.

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:15.730
And, Kaito, the damage you take...

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:19.400
It's 1800!

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:26.120
I now end my turn.

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:29.490
The effect of Cipher Deterrent

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:33.480
doubles Cipher Dragon's attack 
points during the End Phase...

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:39.250
My... My turn!

00:15:41.150 --> 00:15:42.990
This is Sayaka's...

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:45.100
The will of my allies.

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:48.520
It's telling me to soar to greater heights.

00:15:49.650 --> 00:15:53.630
With the will my allies entrusted 
to me, I will fight!

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:55.370
Allies, huh?

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:00.490
I summon Little Fairy!

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:05.510
That's Sayaka's card.

00:16:05.760 --> 00:16:07.250
Little Fairy?

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:09.710
I don't remember that monster from his data...

00:16:10.170 --> 00:16:14.090
Isn't a predictable duel, 
based on data, boring?

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:15.120
What?

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:19.550
To borrow your words, true entertainment 
means surprising people.

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:22.120
You should enjoy this unpredictable duel!

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:28.720
By discarding one card, I can 
increase Little Fairy's level by 1.

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:31.400
I send Cipher Etranger to the graveyard!

00:16:33.370 --> 00:16:36.540
And when Cipher Etranger is 
sent to my graveyard,

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:39.110
I can add one Rank-Up-Magic to my hand.

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:43.840
I activate Rank-Up-Magic Cipher Ascension!

00:16:49.490 --> 00:16:52.140
I target Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon,

00:16:52.140 --> 00:16:55.530
to Xyz Summon a Cipher monster 
of one rank higher.

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:59.230
Rank-Up Xyz Change!

00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:01.970
Galaxy shining in the darkness...

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:06.940
Release your eternal light 
to guide us to the future!

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:13.930
Descend, Rank 9 Neo Galaxy-Eyes 
Cipher Dragon!

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:15.920
Rank 9?

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:17.350
I-Incredible.

00:17:20.110 --> 00:17:23.680
An Xyz Summon that uses 
Cipher Ascension's effect

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:25.710
increases the attack points by 500.

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:28.830
5000 attack points!

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:31.500
What a majestic monster!

00:17:31.840 --> 00:17:36.450
I use all of Neo Galaxy-Eyes 
Cipher Dragon's Overlay Units

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:38.200
to activate its monster effect!

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:40.810
Cipher Super Projection!

00:17:42.690 --> 00:17:47.540
I negate all of your monsters' effects 
and take control of them!

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:51.580
And they all become Neo Galaxy-Eyes 
Cipher Dragons!

00:17:54.070 --> 00:17:57.040
You're just showing off.

00:17:57.040 --> 00:18:01.480
Monsters you take control of with 
that effect can't attack directly.

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:05.520
Which means only the original 
two monsters can attack.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:08.910
But even if you use Neo Galaxy-Eyes's 
5000 attack points

00:18:08.910 --> 00:18:11.980
and Little Fairy's 800 attack 
points to attack directly,

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:16.720
I can still use Bubble Gardna's Pendulum 
Effect to halve the damage.

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:19.680
Then, you're saying that 
even if the attacks hit,

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:21.870
you'll still have life left?

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:22.930
That's right!

00:18:22.930 --> 00:18:24.280
Are you sure about that?

00:18:24.590 --> 00:18:28.680
I activate Continuous Spell 
Cipher Interference!

00:18:30.510 --> 00:18:33.960
I attack directly with Neo Galaxy-Eyes 
Cipher Dragon!

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:36.930
Cipher Interference's effect means

00:18:36.930 --> 00:18:41.170
when two or more monsters, with the same 
name, are on my field during battle,

00:18:41.170 --> 00:18:44.330
the attack points of one double!

00:18:45.980 --> 00:18:47.870
10,000 attack points?

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:50.070
Go, Neo Galaxy-Eyes...

00:18:50.070 --> 00:18:52.240
Terrifying Cipher Stream!

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:30.920
Bravo!

00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:38.610
Damn!

00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:41.900
Slapped down not once, but twice,

00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:44.920
by duelists from the Xyz Dimension...

00:19:44.920 --> 00:19:46.860
What are you doing?

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:51.840
If you don't respond to the applause, 
you'll offend the audience.

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:55.820
Applause is for the victor.

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:58.310
It isn't for a loser like me.

00:19:58.660 --> 00:20:00.360
Goodness me...

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:03.010
But you didn't really lose.

00:20:04.920 --> 00:20:09.990
Dennis, these cheers are 
for both you and Kaito.

00:20:10.450 --> 00:20:13.920
Both of you, together,

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:15.890
brought smiles to all these people.

00:20:19.130 --> 00:20:21.110
It was a brilliant show!

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:25.600
Come with me...

00:20:25.600 --> 00:20:29.040
I'm sure you can make 
even more people smile.

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:30.770
You can change Academia!

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:32.300
I can't do that.

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:38.620
I betrayed Yuya and Kurosaki.

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:40.880
I can't return to them now.

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:41.850
You...

00:20:41.850 --> 00:20:43.430
Don't panic!

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:45.440
I'll tell you where Ruri is.

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:48.560
And the girl named Rin, as well.

00:20:48.560 --> 00:20:50.760
Rin? The one Hugo's looking for?

00:20:50.760 --> 00:20:52.970
They're at the top of the towers.

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:55.980
Rin's at the top of Academia's east tower.

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:57.970
Ruri's at the top of the west tower!

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:03.590
I can't go back to Academia now, either.

00:21:04.050 --> 00:21:07.140
I revealed the Professor's 
greatest secret, after all.

00:21:07.140 --> 00:21:09.850
I'll be praying for you to save them both.

00:21:11.380 --> 00:21:13.610
If you see Yuya, let him know...

00:21:13.610 --> 00:21:17.820
I really enjoyed the days I 
spent with the Lancers.

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:19.020
What are you...

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:24.400
An illusion, my final bit of entertainment.

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:27.560
Witness, as I turn into a card!

00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:28.220
Don't do it!

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:29.240
Dennis!

00:21:47.120 --> 00:21:48.270
Guys!

00:21:48.270 --> 00:21:49.590
Any news?

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:51.020
Nothing here.

00:21:51.020 --> 00:21:52.770
Yeah, out of the question.

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:54.590
No use! I didn't find anything, either!

00:21:55.050 --> 00:21:58.460
There isn't any ship that will let us on?

00:22:00.330 --> 00:22:01.960
Y-You're...

00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:04.510
Serena!

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:06.810
I know a ship.

00:22:06.810 --> 00:22:08.740
Come with me.

00:23:45.730 --> 00:23:48.990
A ship? This is a pirate ship!

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:52.610
Can this thing really take us 
to Academia's island?

00:23:52.610 --> 00:23:54.750
What was that, bucko?

00:23:54.750 --> 00:23:56.120
P-Pirate!

00:23:56.120 --> 00:23:57.260
Allow me to introduce

00:23:57.260 --> 00:23:59.640
the captain of this ship, Captain Solo.

00:23:59.640 --> 00:24:01.690
It may look like a wreck, but it sails fine!

00:24:01.690 --> 00:24:03.210
I guarantee it.

00:24:03.210 --> 00:24:04.460
Are you kidding me?

00:24:04.460 --> 00:24:06.180
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:24:06.690 --> 00:24:10.630
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
Duel Pirate Captain Solo.

00:24:11.010 --> 00:24:13.510
The fun is only getting started!
